# Rust target dir
/target
**/target/

# Cargo lock for libraries — keep only for the binary/firmware
# (cargo lockfiles are committed for binaries by convention)

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
.venv/
.test-venv/
.serena/
.pytest_cache/
*.pyc

# Firmware build artifacts. Nothing produced by a build is committed: the
# flashable image and the ELF are produced by CI (release.yml) or locally by
# build.sh / build-signed.sh, and a committed binary is a binary nobody
# remembers to refresh. CI regenerates the UF2 from the release ELF and gates
# on reproducibility and the flash-budget ratchet instead of on staleness
# against a checked-in copy.
*.uf2
*.elf
# US-1064: the artefact-agreement fixtures are named after the artefact they
# stand in for, because the gate looks for exactly that filename in a release
# directory. These are tiny hand-written stand-ins, not build output.
!tests/scripts/fixtures/agreement/fapico2.uf2
# The sealed image and its OTP config are deployment-specific build outputs
# (produced by build.sh). Regenerate them; never commit a signed artifact or
# the fingerprint it carries.
firmware/fapico2.signed.uf2

# Signing material for RP2350 signed secure boot: the private key plus
# everything derived from it (public key, OTP config, fingerprint). They are
# co-located on purpose — a stale fingerprint beside a new public key is how
# you brick a board with its own firmware.
#
# secrets/README.md is the ONLY thing that belongs in version control here.
# The private key must never reach the repository. The public key, the OTP
# config and the fingerprint are per-developer (build.sh auto-generates a
# key), so they are ignored too; a RELEASE should publish them deliberately
# alongside the image.
secrets/*
!secrets/README.md

# Local build/slop artifacts (POLISH-PUB US-721)
/build/
soak_*.log
*.kh
/.hermes/
.superpowers/

# cargo-cyclonedx per-crate output (only supply-chain/sbom.cdx.json is tracked)
/*.cdx.json
apps/*.cdx.json
apps/*/*.cdx.json
platform/*.cdx.json
vendor/*/*.cdx.json
firmware/*.cdx.json

build-custom.sh

